ogles2.library @RELEASE@ demos for AmigaOS 3.x on PiStorm
==========================================================

Four programs that draw with OpenGL ES 2.0 on the Raspberry Pi's GPU,
through PiStorm and Emu68, ready to run: nothing to install. The library
is in libs/ beside them, and their shaders come compiled for the Pi 4 and
the Pi 3 (shaders/), so no shader compiler is needed.

Requirements
------------
- An Amiga with a PiStorm and a Raspberry Pi 4B or CM4, or a Raspberry Pi
  3B or 3B+
- Emu68 (tested: 1.1.0-beta.1)
- AmigaOS 3.x (tested: 3.2) with Picasso96 or CyberGraphX
- A 32-bit RTG screen for the programs in a window (FULLSCREEN opens a
  screen of its own)

Running them
------------
Unpack the archive anywhere and, from a Shell, in its drawer:

    triangle            a turning coloured triangle in a window
    cube                a textured cube with a depth buffer, in a window
                        you can resize
    boingocean          the Boing ball floating on a ray-marched ocean,
                        all drawn by shaders; drag with the mouse to move
                        the camera, keys 1 to 4 draw it at 1/1 to 1/4 size
    boingocean FULLSCREEN
    boing2026           the 1984 Boing Ball remade: it bounces in a neon
                        room with a soft shadow, a reflecting floor, bloom,
                        4x antialiasing and its "boing" on Paula
    boing2026 TOUR      shows each effect in turn; its keys and options:
                        boing2026.txt

Close the window or press Esc to quit.

Frame rates at 640 x 480, measured on a PiStorm32-lite in an A1200:

                            Pi 4 (2.2 GHz)   Pi 3B (1.2 GHz)
    boingocean                   56               19
    boingocean FULLSCREEN        60               24
    boing2026                    55               15

If they do not start
--------------------
- An older ogles2.library in LIBS: (release 1.3.x, the Pi 4 only) is used
  instead of the one in libs/: on a Pi 3 the programs then do not start.
  Install @RELEASE@ (the archive ogles2-@RELEASE@.lha), or rename the old
  one, then "Avail FLUSH" so the old one leaves memory.
- The library writes what went wrong to T:ogles2.log (or to the file named
  by SetEnv OGLES2/LogFile <file>). Please send it with a report.

More
----
The library, the shader compiler, the installer and the SDK (headers,
import libraries, documentation and these programs' sources) are in
ogles2-@RELEASE@.lha and ogles2-@RELEASE@-sdk.lha.

